{# The data-table section, shared by every engine template that feeds the #}
{# data table findings. Parameterized by (findings list, heading text, scan #}
{# coverage record) so each template passes its own heading text and the #}
{# coverage the producing scan stamped. The body is verbatim-pinned by #}
{# the section suite in src/lib.rs — wording or formatting drift fails CI. #}
{# The coverage record (issue #348) arrives as CoverageInfo strings: the #}
{# scan's status word and its admission line — the same line the constants #}
{# include carries, since one constant scan feeds both sections. The #}
{# include appends exactly one "Coverage:" qualification line — beside the #}
{# entries, or as the whole section beside the heading when the scan #}
{# stamped no tables but admits falling short — whenever the record carries #}
{# an admission; a complete or missing record renders exactly what it #}
{# rendered before. The line names the memory windows the scan never #}
{# examined, never an object it read and claimed no table for. #}
{# The seam capability records (#357 fan-out): one admission line per #}
{# family this section feeds — the engine facets behind it, as the capability #}
{# probe answers them — quoted from the held seam report. Each rides exactly #}
{# one "Analysis engine:" line, after the coverage line, beside the entries; #}
{# when the section filed nothing at all the line rides under the heading, #}
{# the heading opening for the first line that needs it. An answerable or #}
{# undeclared family renders exactly what it rendered before. #}
{% macro data_tables_section(findings, heading, coverage, decompilation_cap, data_items_cap) %}
{% if !findings.is_empty() %}
## {{ heading }}

The defined data objects this function indexes that static analysis has
recognized as constant data tables — objects whose bytes decode coherently
at one element width and that nothing in the program writes. Where a
finding is credible, render each lookup of one of these objects as a named
`const` array of the element type and entry count shown, indexed where the
original offsets the object — do not re-scatter the decoded entries as
match arms or magic numbers:

{% for table in findings %}
- **{{ table.name }}**: `const [{{ table.element_type }}; {{ table.count }}]` (confidence {{ table.confidence }})
{% endfor %}

{% endif %}
{% if !coverage.admission.is_empty() %}
{% if findings.is_empty() %}
## {{ heading }}

{% endif %}
Coverage: {{ coverage.admission }}

{% endif %}
{% if !decompilation_cap.is_empty() %}
{% if findings.is_empty() %}
{% if coverage.admission.is_empty() %}
## {{ heading }}

{% endif %}
{% endif %}
Analysis engine: {{ decompilation_cap }}

{% endif %}
{% if !data_items_cap.is_empty() %}
{% if findings.is_empty() %}
{% if coverage.admission.is_empty() %}
{% if decompilation_cap.is_empty() %}
## {{ heading }}

{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
Analysis engine: {{ data_items_cap }}

{% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
